   "source": [
    "# 🧬⚛️ QTAP: Quantum Torsion Angle Predictor\n",
    "### Variational Quantum Born Machines for Ramachandran Distribution Prediction\n",
    "**Author:** Tommaso R. Marena, Catholic University of America, 2026\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "**Scientific premise:** Protein backbone φ/ψ dihedral distributions are inherently multimodal.\n",
    "Classical point-estimate predictors collapse this structure. This notebook trains a variational\n",
    "quantum Born machine — where Born-rule measurement probabilities *are* the predicted distribution —\n",
    "directly on real PDB torsion angle data, using exact parameter-shift-rule gradients and ADAM optimization.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Pipeline:**\n",
    "1. 📦 Install dependencies\n",
    "2. ⚙️ Configuration\n",
    "3. 🗂️ Fetch real φ/ψ data from RCSB PDB REST API\n",
    "4. 📊 Build empirical Ramachandran reference distributions\n",
    "5. ⚛️ Build variational quantum Born machine circuit\n",
    "6. 🔢 Residue physicochemical feature encoder\n",
    "7. 🔁 Born machine forward pass + parameter-shift gradients\n",
    "8. 🏋️ ADAM training loop with gradient accumulation\n",
    "9. 🤖 Classical MLP baseline (PyTorch)\n",
    "10. 📊 Results comparison table + bootstrap confidence intervals\n",
    "11. 🗺️ Ramachandran heatmap visualization\n",
    "12. 📉 Training convergence curves\n",
    "13. 🔬 Circuit depth & qubit count ablation\n",
    "14. 💾 Save all results\n",
    "\n",
    "> ⏱️ **Runtime:** ~20-40 min on Colab T4 (demo: 4 AAs ~8 min)\n",
    "> ⚠️ **All quantum results are classically simulated via Qiskit Aer**"
   ]
  },
